# TODO

1. Check that a script's requires resolve from what the formula installs. exitor shipped a script requiring http.rb, sys/proctable and SimpleCSV while its install was `bin.install 'bin/exitor'` and nothing else, so a clean install died at the first require; weblink shipped one whose own require_gem shells out to `gem install` at runtime. Both installed cleanly and both were broken. Waits upon audit_requires and vendor_requires being one tool: run per repository with default arguments, audit_requires asks what the repository declares, which for a tap tool is nothing, and reports every vendored gem as undeclared — three false findings on 20260823 and no true ones.
2. Report which vendored files nothing reaches, and which have drifted from the tree they were copied from. 28 in startor and 22 in mercurial reached nothing; startor's MacOS/IfConfig.rb had drifted and was raising. Waits upon the same combination, and upon loading each script's requires in a subprocess.
3. Move secondary_version_findings to the intrinsic side. It compares VERSION.rb and the script header against the formula's version, where the repository already states its version in two places of its own: startor's VERSION.rb at 0.10.0 against a header reading 0.10.2 needed no formula to be seen.
4. A pre-push hook, or something else which runs this without being asked. There are no hooks and no workflows in the tap or in any of the twenty, so every run to date has been by hand.
5. A way to be told that a repository is exempt. A fork carries its upstream's tags, which orphan_findings reports every run: rpm has 87. Likewise a formula retired from the tap with nothing to replace it, which deleted_formula_findings reports every run, Homebrew having nowhere to declare a deletion which was meant.
6. A way to be told that pinning is not yet policy, or accept that pin_finding fires for every unpinned formula until each names a tag.
7. Take the release branch per repository rather than one for all of them. --branch is a single name, so a repository releasing from something else is either told separately or misreported.
8. A way to be told that a repository installs less than it holds. directory_findings reports every tracked directory no install line names, which for namo is comparison/, docs/ and script/ — all three deliberately kept to the clone. Distinct from 5, which exempts a whole repository from a check; this exempts named directories from one check while the rest of the repository is still audited.
9. Report a version which has no CHANGELOG entry at all. summary_findings compares a commit subject against its entry where both exist and says nothing where the entry is absent, so a version can be declared, tagged and released with the changelog never mentioning it. On 20260822 six repositories took a version bump, a tag and a gemspec change with no entry written — coinmarketcap.rb 0.6.2, gate.rb 0.2.1, git.rb 0.14.2, poloniex.rb 0.1.2, statbank_denmark 0.0.1 and stateful 2.3.3 — and nothing reported it for eighteen days. Take the versions from the tags and from the commit subjects which carry one, since either alone misses a version the other has. Find the changelog under CHANGELOG, CHANGELOG.md or CHANGELOG.txt rather than under the one name: all 22 formulae use the first, so the tap alone would never need the others, but matching the exact name `CHANGELOG` is what made the 20260822 sweep pass silently over the six, and a reader which takes any of the three costs nothing and works wherever it is pointed.
